>> title: Young Jackfruit Tacos
>> servings: 4
>> time: 35 minutes
>> tags: exotic, watchme, vegetarian, stovetop, texture

Drain and rinse @young green jackfruit{20%oz} in a #colander{}.

-- watch: Firm triangular cores are separated from the softer shreddable pieces.
Cut away tough cores on a #cutting board{} with a #chef's knife{}.

-- watch: Jackfruit is pulled into strands like shredded meat, not mashed into paste.
Shred the soft jackfruit pieces with your fingers or two #forks{}.

Cook @onion{1/2}, @garlic{2%cloves}, and @neutral oil{1%tbsp} in a #skillet{} until softened, about ~{5%minutes}.

Add jackfruit, @chili powder{2%tsp}, @cumin{1%tsp}, @smoked paprika{1%tsp}, @orange juice{1/2%cup}, and @soy sauce{1%tbsp}.

-- watch: Edges are lightly browned and strands stay distinct.
Simmer and press jackfruit into the pan until saucy and browned in spots, about ~{12%minutes}.

Serve in @corn tortillas{8} with @lime wedges{} and @cilantro{}.
